"""
infer_fusion_tree_3way_stack_cache_miou.py

Airbus Ship Detection — 3-way stacking (candidate-level) with model-based gating (HGBDT)
- detector ensemble -> p_det
- semantic segmentation ensemble -> P_sem (soft map)
- instance segmentation ensemble -> raw candidates (Mask R-CNN masks)
- plus semantic CC candidates from P_sem thresholding
- train HistGradientBoostingClassifier (stacking) to keep/reject each candidate instance.

Added per your requirements:
(2) Make candidate generation more recall-friendly WITHOUT blowing up runtime:
    - soften SemCC thresholds + increase topk (cheap)
    - mild softening for Mask R-CNN score thr (avoid candidate explosion)

(3) Calibrate threshold by Kaggle-aligned multi-IoU average F2:
    - eval_iou_list (default 5 points: 0.50,0.60,0.70,0.80,0.90)
    - compute IoU matrix ONCE and reuse across IoU thresholds

Runtime control:
- Per-image inference caching to avoid repeated model forward:
    cache stores: p_det, lvl, P_sem, inst candidates masks/scores, semCC candidates masks/scores, GT masks (resized)
- Two-stage thr search: coarse (21) + refine (11 around best)

Output:
- submission_tree.csv (variable rows; duplicates ImageId allowed; shipless => exactly one empty row)
- tree_model.pkl, splits.json, meta.json, log_global.txt
- cache/ directory for per-image cached inference results

No pandas, FP32 only.

Requires: scikit-learn, torch, torchvision, PIL, numpy
Optional: opencv-python or scipy (for connected components); fallback is naive BFS.
"""

